Pikachua

Pikachu, small yellow rodent-like Pokémon with soft fur, red cheek patches, long pointed ears with black tips, and a lightning bolt-shaped tail.

He stands alert in a beautiful forest clearing during golden hour, then performs an impressive exhibition electric attack: he lowers his stance, cheeks begin to spark intensely, building up bright crackling energy. Suddenly, he releases a powerful Thunderbolt—massive arcs of bright yellow electricity shoot forward, branching and striking through the air with explosive force. The ground briefly illuminates, nearby trees glow with flashes of light, and the air shimmers with electric energy. Sparks scatter everywhere, and residual lightning dances around his body.

Fluid dynamic motion, realistic physics, natural gravity, electricity illuminating the environment with sharp flashes and dynamic shadows, charged particles and ionized air effects.

